{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nWhile debugging grindable-deviant-angwantibo, a rival mechanism was falsified for that incident but exposed a separate deterministic liveness gap. tests/conftest.py calls tests/_isolation.py::porcelain during pytest_sessionfinish, after pytest has already printed the per-test `[100%]` progress boundary. `porcelain()` launches `git -C <repo> status --porcelain` with no timeout; the sibling `head()` probe is likewise unbounded.\n\n## Runtime proof\nA fake Git that blocked only the second repo-root status call reproduced the exact post-dot boundary. SIGUSR1 captured subprocess.run/_communicate -> tests/_isolation.py:59 porcelain -> tests/conftest.py:681 pytest_sessionfinish. This was not the grindable incident root cause: 100 natural status probes were median 0.0143s, p95 0.0164s, max 0.0610s, while the incident observed stack and discriminating A/B identified pytest numbered-temp cleanup.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a fixed 5-second local watchdog to the read-only repo-isolation Git probes. This is more than 80x the measured 0.0610s maximum and bounds a stuck local child without adding configuration surface.\n- Preserve the existing `None` result for ordinary probe failures/non-repositories, but surface `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` as an explicit isolation-infrastructure failure so timeout can never appear clean.\n- Exercise `porcelain()` through `pytest_sessionfinish` and `head()` through the autouse `_no_repo_commits` per-test commit-guard fixture using deterministic blocking Git shims.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A blocking repo-isolation Git probe cannot keep pytest alive beyond the documented fixed 5-second watchdog.\n- [ ] Timeout produces an explicit isolation-infrastructure failure, never `None`/clean success.\n- [ ] Real `pytest_sessionfinish` and autouse `_no_repo_commits` paths are covered with deterministic subprocess tests.\n- [ ] Normal repo-isolation behavior and the default unit suite remain green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787028206231352001,"uuid":"270c29db-e5bf-4a4c-bb7d-9aea87a5eca8"}